WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.930
Massachusetts, 1812.

2
00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:06.830
Governor Elbridge Gerry approves
a new map of voting districts.

3
00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:10.170
A newspaper says one district
looks like a salamander.

4
00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:13.210
A new word is born: gerrymander.

5
00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:18.470
Every 10 years, the census counts people
and the 435 House seats are shared out

6
00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:19.470
again.

7
00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:24.650
In a made-up state, take 50
voters: 30 Purple, 20 Orange.

8
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:26.490
Split them into five districts of 10.

9
00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:28.870
Now move the lines.

10
00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.010
Are votes just votes,
wherever the lines go?

11
00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:35.090
In this mission, you'll learn
how district lines are redrawn,

12
00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:36.970
and who draws them.

13
00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:38.990
Then you'll test maps of the same voters,

14
00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:41.350
and see what the courts have said.

15
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:45.770
Your mission: decide whether the same
voters can elect different winners just

16
00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:47.310
by moving the lines.
